public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.AutomorphismReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.LocalAction.TwoCoreCentralizer.NormalClosureControl.CentralizerReduction
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.AutomorphismReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.LocalAction.TwoCoreCentralizer.NormalClosureControl.ActionKernel
public import Theory.SpecificGroups.Janko4.Model.AutomorphismReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.LocalAction.TwoCoreCentralizer.NormalClosureControl.IntrinsicCenter

/-!
# Control of the relative max2 seed normal closure

The normal closure of `(XYXYY)^11` inside the subgroup generated by the
certified conjugated max2 outputs is a two-group of exponent dividing four.
`TwoGroup` proves this from the concrete generator relations. `ActionKernel`
puts its relative centralizer inside the normal closure by comparing the
certified presentation bound with the actual outer-action image.
`IntrinsicCenter` then uses the nondegenerate commutator pairing to put this
centralizer in the powers of the distinguished involution. That involution
is central in the local subgroup, so the relative centralizer is exactly its
cyclic subgroup and every centralizing element has square one.

Both centralizer bounds are discharged here. All statements concern the
published normal closure inside `localSubgroup`; identification of this
subgroup with the whole involution centralizer is a separate assertion.

Source motivation: GLS3 Table 5.3i, printed p.270. Concrete source provenance
and the conjugacy bridge are documented in `TwoCoreCentralizer.Max2Bridge`.
-/

public section

namespace Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData

/-- The centralizer of the seed normal closure inside the generated max2 subgroup
is exactly the cyclic subgroup generated by the distinguished involution. -/
theorem localNormalClosure_centralizer_eq_zpowers :
    Subgroup.centralizer (localNormalClosure : Set localSubgroup) =
      Subgroup.zpowers subgroupInvolution :=
  localNormalClosure_centralizer_eq_zpowers_of_bounds
    localNormalClosureAction_ker_le localNormalClosure_inf_centralizer_le_zpowers

/-- Every element of the relative seed centralizer has square one. -/
theorem localNormalClosure_centralizer_pow_two :
    ∀ z ∈ Subgroup.centralizer (localNormalClosure : Set localSubgroup), z ^ 2 = 1 :=
  localNormalClosure_centralizer_pow_two_of_bounds
    localNormalClosureAction_ker_le localNormalClosure_inf_centralizer_le_zpowers

end Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData
